IMPORT prelude

-- Jurong Town Corporation Act 1968 (Singapore) -- the Corporation's board and its limits (ss 5, 8, 9), what needs the Minister's
-- or the President's approval (ss 12(4)(l)-(n), 13(4), (5)), spending only against a budget (s 24), the offences and penalties
-- (ss 27, 33, 35, 35A, 35C), entry for statistics (s 35D), composition (s 67), and the Corporation's capped liability for goods
-- at Jurong Port (ss 57, 59-62).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/JTCA1968.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amending Act annotated is 27/2019.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 8 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content.
-- Not encoded: definitions beyond those used, appointments and terms of office, working capital, shares (s 14A), budget and
-- accounts procedure (ss 15-18, 21, 23), investment (s 26), registration of land sales (s 31), regulations (s 32), the 1968 EDB
-- transfer (s 34), service of notices (ss 35A(2)-(6), 66), the 2018 transfer of HDB's industrial undertaking (Part 4), the
-- s 58 port liability contract, conduct of prosecutions (s 65), and the symbols in the Schedule.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Jurong Town Corporation Act 1968`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `5 -- constitution, quorum and interested members`

-- s 5(1): the Corporation consists of "(a) a Chairperson; and (b) not fewer than 4 and not more than 14 other members".
-- s 5(3): "The quorum at all meetings of the Corporation is 4 or one-third of the total number of members in office, whichever is
-- the higher."
-- s 5(8): a member "must not ... participate in any discussion relating to, and must not vote in respect of, any business in which
-- the member is interested, and if the member does so the member's vote must not be counted nor is the member counted in the
-- quorum".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board size is within the Act` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 4 AND `other members` AT MOST 14

-- "Members in office" is read as including the Chairperson (the Corporation "consists of" both). That is an inference.
GIVEN `members in office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quorum` MEANS
    `the higher of` 4 (`members in office` DIVIDED BY 3)

GIVEN `members in office` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER, `interested members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate on the business` IF
    (`members present` MINUS `interested members present`) AT LEAST `the quorum` `members in office`

§§ `8 -- delegation`

-- s 8(2): to a committee or the Chairperson, "all or any of the powers ... except the power to borrow money or to raise loans by
-- the issue of bonds and debentures". s 8(3): to any employee, the same "except the power to borrow money or to raise loans".
DECLARE Delegate IS ONE OF
    `a committee`
    `the Chairperson`
    `an employee`

DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `borrowing money`
    `raising a loan by issuing bonds`
    `leasing land`
    `awarding a scholarship to an employee`

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate, `the power` IS A Power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power may be delegated` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `borrowing money` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `raising a loan by issuing bonds` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `9 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 9(1): nothing done by a member or employee "or any other person acting under the direction of the Corporation" shall, "if the
-- matter or thing was done ... bona fide for the purpose of executing the provisions of this Act", subject that person personally
-- to any action, liability, claim or demand.
GIVEN `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted to execute the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is protected from personal liability` IF
    `acted in good faith` AND `acted to execute the Act`

§§ `12(4)(l)-(n), 13(4), (5) -- what needs approval`

-- s 12(4): the Corporation may "(d) sell or lease land and premises ... upon terms that the Corporation may determine"; "(k) provide
-- loans on mortgage ... to enable persons, other than employees ... to purchase" a home; "(l) with the Minister's written approval,
-- form or participate in the formation of a company ... or enter into any joint venture or partnership"; "(m) with the Minister's
-- written approval, grant loans to any company in which the Corporation or any of its subsidiary companies holds any shares";
-- "(n) with the written approval of the Minister and the President, guarantee the repayment of loans given to" such a company.
DECLARE Venture IS ONE OF
    `selling or leasing land`
    `a mortgage loan to a home buyer`
    `forming a company or joint venture`
    `lending to a company it holds shares in`
    `guaranteeing a loan to a company it holds shares in`

GIVEN `the venture` IS A Venture, `the Minister approved in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President approved in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may proceed` IF
    CONSIDER `the venture`
    WHEN `forming a company or joint venture` THEN `the Minister approved in writing`
    WHEN `lending to a company it holds shares in` THEN `the Minister approved in writing`
    WHEN `guaranteeing a loan to a company it holds shares in` THEN `the Minister approved in writing` AND `the President approved in writing`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 13(4): bonds and debentures "issued before 1 October 1994 are guaranteed by the Government"; (5): those issued on or after that
-- date are guaranteed "if the President, acting in the President's discretion, concurs with the giving of such guarantee".
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `issued on` IS A NUMBER, `the President concurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bond is Government-guaranteed` IF
    `issued on` LESS THAN 19941001 OR `the President concurred`

§§ `24 -- payments only against the budget`

-- s 24(1): "A payment must not be made by the Corporation unless the expenditure is covered by an item in a budget and a sufficient
-- balance for the item is available." (2): despite that, it may pay (a) deposits that have become repayable; (b) sums credited in
-- error; (c) sums under a Collector of Land Revenue award, land acquisition law, or "any judgment or order of any court"; (d)
-- expenditure which "in the opinion of the Corporation, cannot be postponed". (3): "Provision must be made in a supplemental budget
-- for any payment made under subsection (2)(c) or (d)."
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `ordinary expenditure`
    `a deposit that has become repayable`
    `a sum credited in error`
    `a court judgment or land acquisition award`
    `expenditure that cannot be postponed`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment, `covered by a budget item` IS A BOOLEAN, `sufficient balance on the item` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment may be made` IF
        (`covered by a budget item` AND `sufficient balance on the item`)
    OR  CONSIDER `the payment`
        WHEN `ordinary expenditure` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment, `covered by a budget item` IS A BOOLEAN, `sufficient balance on the item` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a supplemental budget must provide for it` IF
        (NOT (`covered by a budget item` AND `sufficient balance on the item`))
    AND CONSIDER `the payment`
        WHEN `a court judgment or land acquisition award` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `expenditure that cannot be postponed` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `27(3)-(5) -- identity on suspicion of breaching the Corporation's rules`

-- s 27(3): the Corporation or an authorised employee "who reasonably believes that any person has committed an offence under any
-- rules made under this section may require the person to furnish evidence of the person's identity". (4): an offence to "(a)
-- without reasonable excuse, refuse[] to furnish" it or "(b) wilfully misstate[]" it -- fine up to $5,000. (5): a person "is not
-- excused ... on the ground that to do so might tend to incriminate the person".
GIVEN `refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `the only excuse is self-incrimination` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully misstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the identity offence is committed` IF
        (`refused` AND (NOT (`had a reasonable excuse` AND (NOT `the only excuse is self-incrimination`))))
    OR  `wilfully misstated`

§§ `35A(7) -- statistical returns`

-- s 35A(1): the Corporation may by notice require any person to furnish particulars "for the purpose of obtaining statistical
-- information in relation to industrial property in Singapore". (7): an offence if the person "(a) wilfully refuses or without
-- lawful excuse (the proof of which lies on the person) neglects to furnish" within the time, or "(b) wilfully furnishes ... any
-- false particulars".
GIVEN `wilfully refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `neglected to furnish in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully furnished false particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statistical return offence is committed` IF
        `wilfully refused`
    OR  (`neglected to furnish in time` AND (NOT `proved a lawful excuse`))
    OR  `wilfully furnished false particulars`

§§ `35C -- secrecy of statistical information`

-- s 35C(1): a member, officer or employee "must not disclose" information obtained under s 35A or 35B unless (a) with the "previous
-- written consent" of the person who furnished it or to whom it relates; (b) "in the form of statistics which do not identify" the
-- person; (c) to the URA on a request under s 44A of its Act; (d) to the Chief Statistician under s 6 of the Statistics Act 1973
-- "where the particulars or information is not exempted under section 6(2)"; (e) for proceedings for an offence under s 35A(7) or
-- s 35C; or (f) "already in the public domain". (4): nothing in (1) authorises disclosure "to any officer or employee of the
-- Corporation not charged with any duties or function under section 35A or 35B". (3): $2,000 or one year or both.
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `with the furnisher's prior written consent`
    `as statistics identifying no one`
    `to the URA on its s 44A request`
    `to the Chief Statistician, not exempted`
    `to the Chief Statistician, exempted under s 6(2)`
    `for an offence prosecution under s 35A(7) or s 35C`
    `of information already public`
    `to a colleague with no s 35A or 35B duties`
    `to a property developer`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `to the Chief Statistician, exempted under s 6(2)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to a colleague with no s 35A or 35B duties` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to a property developer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `35D -- entry to obtain statistics`

-- s 35D: an authorised officer may, "at any reasonable time, with the consent of the occupier ... or after 6 hours' previous
-- notice to such an occupier, and without involving any search or seizure", enter land or premises (a) to obtain statistical
-- information on industrial property or (b) to verify particulars furnished under s 35A(1).
GIVEN `authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN, `occupier consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of notice` IS A NUMBER, `involves search or seizure` IS A BOOLEAN, `for statistics or verification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is authorised` IF
        `authorised officer`
    AND `at a reasonable time`
    AND (`occupier consented` OR `hours of notice` AT LEAST 6)
    AND (NOT `involves search or seizure`)
    AND `for statistics or verification`

§§ `27(2)(b), 27(4), 33, 35(3), 35A(7), 35C(3), 67 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 27(2)(b): rules may make a contravention "an offence punishable by a fine not exceeding $5,000". s 27(4): fine up to $5,000.
-- s 33: obstructing or refusing access to an officer -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 6 months" (no "or to both"). s 35(3): using a symbol resembling the Corporation's "as to or be likely to deceive or cause
-- confusion" -- $2,000 or 6 months or both. s 35A(7): $2,000 or 6 months or both. s 35C(3): $2,000 or one year or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `breaching a rule made under s 27`
    `refusing identity under s 27(4)`
    `obstructing an officer under s 33`
    `misusing the Corporation's symbol under s 35(3)`
    `failing a statistical return under s 35A(7)`
    `unlawful disclosure under s 35C(3)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Corporation's symbol under s 35(3)` THEN 2000
    WHEN `failing a statistical return under s 35A(7)` THEN 2000
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure under s 35C(3)` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer under s 33` THEN 6
    WHEN `misusing the Corporation's symbol under s 35(3)` THEN 6
    WHEN `failing a statistical return under s 35A(7)` THEN 6
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure under s 35C(3)` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fine and imprisonment may be combined` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Corporation's symbol under s 35(3)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `failing a statistical return under s 35A(7)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure under s 35C(3)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 67(1): the chief executive officer or an authorised officer may compound an offence "that is prescribed as a compoundable
-- offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of ... (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for
-- the offence; (b) $5,000". (2): on payment "no further proceedings are to be taken". (4): sums go into the Consolidated Fund.
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition ceiling` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition ceiling for` MEANS
    `the composition ceiling` (`the maximum fine` `the offence`)

§§ `57, 59-62 -- the Corporation's liability for goods at Jurong Port`

-- s 57: the Corporation is not liable "(a) for any loss ... by reason of misdelivery, short delivery or non-delivery of any goods"
-- in its custody "other than transhipment goods and goods accepted for storage"; nor "(b) for damage to or destruction of any goods
-- ... in the sum of more than $2,000 per package or unit unless the nature and value of the goods ... have, prior to delivery ...
-- been declared in writing", and "shall not in any event be liable therefor where the value of those goods has been misstated".
-- s 59: for transhipment goods it is liable "from the time of acknowledgment of the receipt ... until delivery ... alongside the
-- on-carrying vessel", subject to s 60, with the same $2,000 cap and misstatement rule.
-- s 60: no liability for loss arising from "(a) fire or flood, unless caused by the actual fault or privity of the Corporation;
-- (b) an act of God; ... (g) strikes ...; (j) insufficient or improper packing ...; (m) the dangerous nature of those goods", among
-- others. s 61(2): exempt from all liability for cargo subject to a declaration of general or particular average. s 62: exempt for
-- "any act, omission or default of the stevedore or workman", who is deemed the vessel owner's employee even if paid by the
-- Corporation.
-- Goods accepted for storage under s 63 are outside this rule and are not modelled.
DECLARE Goods IS ONE OF
    `transhipment goods`
    `other goods`

DECLARE Loss IS ONE OF
    `damage or destruction`
    `misdelivery or non-delivery`

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `ordinary handling`
    `fire caused by the Corporation's actual fault`
    `fire without the Corporation's fault`
    `an act of God`
    `a strike`
    `insufficient packing`
    `the dangerous nature of the goods`
    `cargo under a general average declaration`
    `a stevedore's default`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cause excludes liability` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `ordinary handling` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `fire caused by the Corporation's actual fault` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `value of the package` IS A NUMBER, `value declared in writing beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN, `value misstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the capped amount` MEANS
    IF `value misstated` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `value declared in writing beforehand` THEN `value of the package`
         ELSE `the lower of` `value of the package` 2000

-- The result is the most the Act leaves the Corporation open to per package; s 57 limits liability rather than creating it.
GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods, `the loss` IS A Loss, `the cause` IS A Cause, `value of the package` IS A NUMBER, `value declared in writing beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN, `value misstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Corporation can be liable for per package` MEANS
    IF `the cause excludes liability` `the cause` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the goods` EQUALS `other goods` AND `the loss` EQUALS `misdelivery or non-delivery` THEN 0
         ELSE `the capped amount` `value of the package` `value declared in writing beforehand` `value misstated`
